nt of  vitamin b12  and that is why many vegan people  are actually deficient of vitamin b12  because plant sources doesn't have as  high as a  vitamin b12 compared to the animal  sources  now poor people around the world doesn't  have access to money to buy good quality  of meat in a daily basis that is why  most likely they could also be uh  deficient for vitamin b12 and that is  why the third world country is the  place where there are many people with  malnutrition and there is an overall  deficiency of vitamin b12  absorption of vitamin b12 is a complex  process  anyway there are two important steps for  example parietal cell secretes castles  intrinsic factor  which is important for the absorption  process further down the intestine  there are specific receptors which  actually binds to these uh  conjugated vitamin b12 and leads to its  absorption  now there could be problems in this  absorption process which might lead to a  problem  for example atrophic gastritis in which  your stomach lining get thinned is a  problem where you can't have vitamin b12  absorption  conditions that affect your small  intestines such as crohn's disease  celiac disease bacterial growth  parasitic infection all of this can  possibly  reduce the chance of vitamin b12  in the in this team alcohol consumption  and alcohol abuse is another  reason for which the vitamin b12  absorption might be abbreviated  other than that pernicious anemia is  another situation where the absorption  is disrupted  now we understood that what are the  causes of deficiency let's try to  understand what are the effects of  deficiency or what is what are the  pathological situations  first of all there are metabolic  consequences because vitamin b12 is  important for metabolism  several enzymes that are required for  important biochemical pathway use  vitamin b12 as a coenzyme  for example  isomerase  methyl transferase dehalogenase all of  these enzymes actually use vitamin b12  for their functioning  so 